At Viettel Post, candidates will have the opportunity to work in a dynamic, youthful, and professional environment, accompanied by the following attractive benefits:
1. Compensation and Benefits
Competitive salary based on individual capability and agreement;
Additional allowances for phone expenses and lunch, along with annual company-sponsored vacation trips;
Performance and holiday bonuses awarded on major national and corporate occasions (e.g., April 30th, May 1st, September 2nd, Viettel Group and Corporation founding anniversaries, Gregorian and Lunar New Year);
Opportunities for frequent international business trips, working in a multicultural environment, and directly contributing to the global expansion of Viettel Post’s business network.
(For long-term overseas assignments, income will follow a separate compensation scheme applicable to local markets.)
2. Healthcare Programs
Full coverage of statutory insurance: social insurance, health insurance, and unemployment insurance, along with additional healthcare insurance packages;
Annual health check-ups for all employees;
Additional daily time off: Female employees with children under one year of age are entitled to an extra one hour of leave per day.
3. Engaging Collective Activities
A wide range of team-building and corporate activities are regularly organized to foster connection and a positive workplace culture.

